@host = http://localhost:5129
@jane = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@arjun = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@david = 20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@sarah = 30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Health
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Seeded demo users (no header needed)
GET {{host}}/api/users

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/users/me
X-User-Id: {{jane}}

### Claimant submits a claim -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/claims
X-User-Id: {{jane}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimType": "Motor",
  "description": "Rear-ended while stopped at a traffic light.",
  "incidentLocation": "Orchard Road, Singapore",
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-20T09:30:00+08:00",
  "claimedAmount": 4500.50,
  "marketCode": "SG"
}

### Invalid payload -> 400 with field errors
POST {{host}}/api/claims
X-User-Id: {{jane}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimType": "Property",
  "description": "Pipe burst in kitchen.",
  "incidentLocation": "Kuala Lumpur",
  "incidentDate": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "claimedAmount": 1.234,
  "marketCode": "US"
}

### Officer tries to submit -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/claims
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimType": "Property",
  "description": "Pipe burst in kitchen.",
  "incidentLocation": "Kuala Lumpur",
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
  "claimedAmount": 100,
  "marketCode": "MY"
}

### Claimant's own claims (newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/claims
X-User-Id: {{jane}}

### Another claimant sees none of Jane's claims
GET {{host}}/api/claims
X-User-Id: {{arjun}}

### Officer work queue: unassigned, submitted, Singapore (oldest first)
GET {{host}}/api/claims?assignment=Unassigned&status=Submitted&marketCode=SG
X-User-Id: {{david}}

### Claim detail (replace the id with one returned above)
GET {{host}}/api/claims/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-User-Id: {{david}}

### No header -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/claims

### Team dashboard (officer or manager) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard
X-User-Id: {{sarah}}

### Dashboard as claimant -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard
X-User-Id: {{jane}}

### Jane's notifications (created asynchronously from Kafka claim-events)
GET {{host}}/api/notifications
X-User-Id: {{jane}}

#######################################################################
### WORKFLOW — run top to bottom. Set @claimId from the submit response,
### Each step shows the version it expects (it goes up by 1 per successful action).
#######################################################################
@claimId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@requestId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@mei = 20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### 1. David picks up (version 0) -> UnderReview
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/pick-up
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 0 }

### 1b. Mei tries with the same stale version -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/pick-up
X-User-Id: {{mei}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 0 }

### 2. David sets reserve (version 1)
PUT {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/reserve
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 1, "amount": 4000 }

### 3. David requests information (version 2) -> AdditionalInformationRequired
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/information-requests
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 2, "question": "Please provide the police report number." }

### 4. Jane responds (version 3) -> UnderReview. Set @requestId from informationRequests[0].id
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/information-requests/{{requestId}}/response
X-User-Id: {{jane}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 3, "response": "Police report SG-12345." }

### 5a. Approve more than claimed -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/approve
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 4, "approvedAmount": 999999, "reason": "Too generous" }

### 5. David approves (version 4) -> Approved
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/approve
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 4, "approvedAmount": 4200, "reason": "Covered under policy; excess deducted." }

### 6. David settles (version 5) -> Settled
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/settle
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 5 }

### Alternative: reject (from UnderReview or AdditionalInformationRequired)
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/reject
X-User-Id: {{david}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 4, "reason": "Incident falls under a policy exclusion." }
